<chapter xml:id="ch-coordinate-geometry" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Coordinate Geometry</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Coordinate geometry connects algebra and geometry by placing shapes on a grid.
      Every point is described by an ordered pair <m>(x, y)</m>, and we can calculate distances, midpoints, and slopes algebraically.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="gt07_coordinates.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="gt08_midpoint-distance.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="gt09_slope.ptx" />

</chapter>
